WEBVTT

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:09.560
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:12.450
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.290
but also in crime.

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:16.410
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:20.130
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:23.600
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:49.480
moshimo ima anata no yume no eria ga
Should the area of your dreams

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:54.580
namida ni okasare
Be invaded now by tears

00:00:55.540 --> 00:01:01.790
kujiketa toki wa nee kokoro de
When I faltered, in my heart

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:07.790
watashi no namae yonde
My name calls

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:12.810
hurry up hurry up ai no tsubasa
Hurry up, hurry up, the wings of love

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:19.800
anata no sora e tonde yuku
Will fly to your sky

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:23.890
I’m gonna fly fly away

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.890
KONDISHON GUURIN
Condition green

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:32.980
mukai kanashimi wo tasuketai no
Do you want to help this deep sorrow?

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:35.990
Just fly fly away

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:42.370
onaji itami wo mune no REDAA wa
The radar of your heart

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:48.380
itsu demo kanjite iru wa
Is always feeling the same pain

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:54.720
Just I'm gonna fly away

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:18.070
Hurry!

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:48.150
The Men Who Returned

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:55.530
Shinobu?

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:58.290
I'll be out for a while.

00:02:58.290 --> 00:02:59.290
How long?

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:02.210
That depends on him.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:07.080
Yes, of course. Have fun.

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:08.380
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:10.010
See you later.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:30.790
Definitely a Labor,
and a large one, at that.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:32.400
I know that!

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:38.660
This is their third operation.
They're causing a lot of damage.

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:40.160
Yes, I see that.

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:51.160
Chief Fukushima,
of Special Vehicles?

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:54.970
No, I'm only Goto.
This is the Chief.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:58.000
Any leads yet?

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:03.390
We're matching the paint
residue against known Labors.

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:05.980
We'll have a match in a day or so.

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:09.860
Are you going to test
all 8000 Labors in Tokyo?

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.530
I guess we'll have to,
if that's what it takes.

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:16.990
There's a slight chance we'll
need Special Vehicles' help.

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:19.280
A slight chance?

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:22.360
Is there a slight chance
they'll strike again?

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:28.750
Personally, I hope so.
We could use a few more clues.

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:29.950
What's that?

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:32.410
Oh? You mean the graffiti?

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:34.540
Oh, never mind.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.400
Is there something odd about it?

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:40.140
I dunno. Let me think about it...

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:01.950
Hey, you want one?

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:07.660
I'll take all your pandas.

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:15.800
Oh, thank you.

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:23.180
Monkey Mountain.

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:33.860
Maybe next time, okay?

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:37.320
Let's go.

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:39.070
Right.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:45.620
Monkey Mountain

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.300
Sarusuberi!

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:03.170
Did you see the paper?
We made the headlines!

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:06.310
Idiot!
We have to be careful!

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:09.560
I'm sorry.
I just felt so proud.

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:13.060
You should imagine cops hiding
behind every corner. Be careful!

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:19.530
No, I imagine there are thieves
hiding behind every corner!

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:21.310
What did I just tell you?

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:25.820
I should be careful?
Oh! I get it!

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:28.200
I shouldn't talk so much in public.

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:29.280
Idiot!

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:32.160
I'm doing my best.

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:39.090
He who lives without folly
isn't as wise as he thinks.

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:41.050
De la Rochefoucauld.

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:43.630
Who wants ice cream?

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:47.560
Good idea. I'll go buy it.

00:06:53.190 --> 00:07:01.860
Besides, you said everything
up to now was small potatoes.

00:07:02.570 --> 00:07:04.870
I'm asking one more time!

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:06.700
Thank you very much, sir!

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.080
Come on.

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:14.790
Here you go.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:20.450
I have strawberry, chocolate,
and vanilla. Which do you want?

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:21.630
Mint.

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:24.010
Stop sniveling.

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:27.350
And you, Sarusuberi?

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:29.510
Strawberry.

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:34.270
Oh, well.

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:42.990
This isn't bad for
something with no color.

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:45.280
Neko, I'm pulling one more job.

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:46.680
What?

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:51.100
One last ATM, but a much
larger amount this time.

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:57.160
But Itchoku, if they catch you
again, you'll never get out!

00:07:57.390 --> 00:08:04.220
We'd still be in jail
if Sarusuberi hadn't bailed us out!

00:08:04.220 --> 00:08:06.130
I paid him back yesterday.

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:09.260
Then we're fine.
Stop talking crazy.

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:11.640
You talk too much.

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:16.980
That's true.

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:20.930
Are you in?

00:08:21.110 --> 00:08:24.650
We must dare, and dare
again, and dare for ever.

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:28.160
Georges-Jacques Danton.
I'm in.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:34.410
Two against one.
That's it.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:48.090
Wait! Wait for me! Don't leave
me behind! Wait up, Itchoku!

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:03.010
It sure is hot today.

00:09:03.010 --> 00:09:05.900
I wish we were mobilizing instead.

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:13.200
Ota can't take the stress.

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:16.790
Let him be.
So where's Division 1?

00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:19.620
There was a burglary in Nagayoshi.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:21.330
A burglary?

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:24.300
Same M.O. as our case.

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:28.380
They thought that using a
Labor would get them a ton of cash.

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:32.170
There are too many stupid people.

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:35.360
But our suspects haven't
shown up in a while.

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:37.020
Fine by me.

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:44.140
Captain's Office

00:09:43.070 --> 00:09:44.140
May I come in?

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:49.570
That's the most popular
model in Thailand.

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:55.870
Thanks, if you find out
anything more, please let us know.

00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:02.500
Are those the
suspects in the ATM case?

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:11.840
Mind if I take a look?

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:20.270
Drop this one and this one.
They don't match the M.O.

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:32.320
These two both work alone.
It's not their usual style either,

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:36.350
but mainly they're loners.
This was a group job.

00:10:36.350 --> 00:10:39.570
So they couldn't pull
it off by themselves?

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:40.750
That's my thinking.

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:50.550
What does this look like to you?

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:52.740
Some sort of smiley face?

00:10:52.740 --> 00:10:54.880
It looks like a monkey to me.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:55.590
A monkey?

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:58.350
You know, it seems
vaguely familiar.

00:10:58.350 --> 00:11:03.390
My memory's gotten so
bad lately. It must be my age.

00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:27.660
Where is he? He's such a pain!

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:31.550
Only the patient can hope
to master a truly difficult task.

00:11:31.550 --> 00:11:34.380
Friedrich Von Shiller.
Be patient.

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:37.470
I've had it.
I'm going to go find him.

00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:42.060
Itchoku Inubashiri?
I have a few questions for you.

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:46.230
Sorry, I don't know the man.
You've got the wrong guy.

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:49.320
Did I surprise you?

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:57.950
It was just a joke! I'm sorry!
I was just kidding! I'm sorry.

00:11:57.950 --> 00:12:00.490
Your jokes are totally pathetic!

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:05.700
An idiot like you will never make a good
criminal! You've got to be more careful!

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:07.140
Yes.

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:09.210
Itchoku, lower your voice.

00:12:16.390 --> 00:12:19.220
Sarusuberi!

00:12:37.030 --> 00:12:38.500
You can't be serious!

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:39.740
Yup.

00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:42.180
No chance.
That place is bad news.

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:43.790
It'll be fine.

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:46.210
It's too close to police HQ!

00:12:46.210 --> 00:12:50.500
It's jinxed! You tried it
and failed three years ago.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:52.840
It'll take the police
ten minutes to respond.

00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:56.570
We'll be gone in
three minutes. Plenty of leeway.

00:12:56.570 --> 00:12:59.340
If everything follows the plan.

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:01.710
The Furukawa job
took seven minutes.

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:10.980
Optimism is the faith that
leads to achievement. Helen Keller.

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:12.680
We can do it.

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:15.890
Sarusuberi.

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:18.860
So what happened three years ago?

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:20.780
You don't need to know.

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:21.990
Meanie.

00:13:22.450 --> 00:13:24.200
Only to you.

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:26.400
Cut it out.

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:31.330
Hello, this is Goto.
Yes, it's been a while, hasn't it?

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:36.370
I need a favor.

00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:39.380
Oh, come on. Just a little favor.

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:44.220
We planted this
same bomb once before.

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:46.470
Is that why you're against it?

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:48.560
Exactly. It <i>won't</i> work.

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:51.370
I'm sorry. I'll be quiet.

00:13:51.370 --> 00:13:54.980
The casing, setup, and
execution were flawless.

00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:56.610
The job was perfect.

00:13:56.610 --> 00:13:59.050
So why did you fail?

00:13:59.050 --> 00:14:01.700
The timer didn't work.

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:04.390
The bomb never went off.

00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:05.360
Then...

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:07.390
How do you rate our chances?

00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:10.730
Fifty-fifty. My reputation
can handle it either way.

00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:13.330
The Kasumigaseki building.
When?

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:15.130
This Thursday.

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:19.620
So what about it?

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:21.290
You remember it?

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:26.110
Of course! We lucked out.
If that bomb had gone off...

00:14:26.110 --> 00:14:29.550
I believe there was some
odd graffiti there, too.

00:14:29.770 --> 00:14:32.260
What do you mean, "too?"

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:36.320
Like at every ATM crime scene.

00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:37.600
Really?

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:40.530
Or perhaps it's just kids
doing chalk drawings.

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:52.120
You have a lead?

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:55.440
It looks like Sankichi
Sarusuberi is back.

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:58.490
He was the ringleader three
years ago. Why's he back?

00:14:58.490 --> 00:15:03.890
Maybe the "Home of the Sea"
gang is planning something big.

00:15:07.430 --> 00:15:08.890
Excuse me.

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:14.190
This is a sketch of the man
who posted Inubashiri's bail.

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:24.940
A definite resemblance.

00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:39.290
Hey Itchoku, what if I have
to go to the bathroom?

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:41.670
Why didn't you go before we left?

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:46.010
I'm fine right now.
I mean, when you're gone.

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:47.340
Just hold it!

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:50.050
What if I can't?

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:53.550
I will never understand how
<i>you</i> managed to hijack a plane!

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:57.650
Y-yeah, I was pretty amazing, wasn't I?

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:03.860
The die is cast. Julius Caesar.

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:04.740
Roger.

00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:19.880
Neko, I'm counting on you.

00:16:23.380 --> 00:16:30.010
The bank is closed.
We open at 9 A.M.

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:35.430
This is private property.
Customers may not enter.

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:37.010
Please stop!

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:39.400
Sorry, I'm not a customer.

00:16:42.530 --> 00:16:43.860
Dog

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:52.150
This will give me a
little pocket money.

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:54.250
<i>A guard! Be careful!</i>

00:16:55.790 --> 00:16:58.170
What do you think you're doing?

00:16:58.500 --> 00:17:00.870
Sorry, no time for chit-chat.

00:17:03.170 --> 00:17:04.800
Where are the police?

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:11.050
They're five minutes
ahead of schedule!

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:11.890
<i>Roger!</i>

00:17:14.390 --> 00:17:16.140
Over here!

00:17:19.440 --> 00:17:21.110
Hurry! Hurry!

00:17:22.940 --> 00:17:27.150
Attention, Labor! Halt and exit
your vehicle immediately!

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:30.660
They mobilized way too quickly.

00:17:39.960 --> 00:17:42.540
<i>This is our chance.
Break through and escape!</i>

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:44.630
Itchoku, hurry!

00:17:53.140 --> 00:17:54.260
Impossible!

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:15.960
There's no escape!

00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:17.410
What?

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:22.170
Ota!

00:18:28.380 --> 00:18:29.720
Neko, get out of here!

00:18:31.180 --> 00:18:33.010
Take the money and run!

00:18:33.010 --> 00:18:34.300
<i>But...</i>

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:36.470
Just don't drop the money!

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:39.630
Itchoku, I'm sorry!

00:18:40.020 --> 00:18:41.350
Stop it!

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:46.610
I don't think so!

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:51.030
What are you doing?

00:18:51.030 --> 00:18:52.520
<i>He's fast.</i>

00:18:52.520 --> 00:18:56.450
Forget the Labor, stop the truck!

00:19:02.710 --> 00:19:03.500
What?

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:04.450
<i>There he goes!</i>

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:08.300
Halt!

00:19:14.220 --> 00:19:16.140
He's gone!

00:19:20.060 --> 00:19:22.140
Sarusuberi, Itchoku is...

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:24.390
Itchoku, abandon your Labor.

00:19:24.390 --> 00:19:27.110
<i>Without it, we can't open the ATM.</i>

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:29.070
Forget the money!

00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:29.900
<i>What</i>?

00:19:29.900 --> 00:19:33.900
Just get out of there!
Don't let them catch you!

00:19:37.950 --> 00:19:39.450
On your left, Noa.

00:19:44.330 --> 00:19:49.550
Attention Boxer Pilot. Exit your
cockpit immediately. I repeat...

00:19:49.550 --> 00:19:53.420
Attention Boxer Pilot.
Exit your cockpit immediately.

00:19:55.590 --> 00:19:57.480
Noa, wait a minute.

00:19:57.480 --> 00:19:58.830
What's the matter?

00:19:58.830 --> 00:20:01.180
Something's not right.
Be careful.

00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:11.650
He's gone.

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:14.150
He tricked us.

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:25.670
They found the truck
and all the cash.

00:20:25.670 --> 00:20:29.500
It was at a construction site,
only a five minute walk away.

00:20:30.210 --> 00:20:33.010
They even ignored a
"No Trespassing" sign.

00:20:33.010 --> 00:20:35.630
What about the criminals?

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:38.260
They must have escaped on foot.

00:20:38.850 --> 00:20:43.310
Sarusuberi must be
aching for a return match.

00:20:43.310 --> 00:20:47.980
Probably. How did you know that
last night would be the night?

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:50.150
Well, today is Friday, right?

00:20:50.150 --> 00:20:51.140
Yeah.

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:55.820
More people make withdrawals
on Friday, leaving less cash.

00:20:55.820 --> 00:21:01.030
Thursday's machine was a better
target, since it had more cash.

00:21:01.240 --> 00:21:04.290
Are you just making that up?

00:21:04.290 --> 00:21:05.370
Yes.

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:07.300
Captain!

00:21:07.300 --> 00:21:13.080
That explanation should help
the night watchman sleep easier.

00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:30.490
Well, that's the way
the cookie crumbles.

00:21:30.490 --> 00:21:31.400
Yah.

00:21:42.830 --> 00:21:44.040
Still...

00:21:45.790 --> 00:21:48.000
I don't feel too bad.

00:21:58.550 --> 00:21:59.880
See you later.

00:21:59.880 --> 00:22:03.180
Sarusuberi, thank
you for everything.

00:22:05.430 --> 00:22:08.180
Wherever you go,
take care of yourself.

00:22:08.350 --> 00:22:09.980
You too, Neko.

00:22:09.980 --> 00:22:11.100
Let's go, Neko.

00:22:11.100 --> 00:22:12.360
Yup.

00:22:13.400 --> 00:22:14.440
Bye.

00:22:33.670 --> 00:22:38.390
Friends and wine are both
best when old. English proverb.

00:22:38.390 --> 00:22:40.220
See you again.

00:23:00.150 --> 00:23:05.160
arashi ga itsushika owatta
When I looked out, the storm had passed a long time ago.

00:23:06.240 --> 00:23:12.920
yuube no kobushi wa kirei ni
The morning dew betrays how yesterday's...

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:15.100
arawareta
sorrows have been washed away.

00:23:15.100 --> 00:23:20.340
yoake ga NEJI wo yurumereba
Dawn is let loose by unbolting the panels of night.

00:23:21.220 --> 00:23:28.590
MASHIN ya BIRU ga mezameru
Even machines and the buildings all wake up.

00:23:28.590 --> 00:23:30.300
I got it

00:23:30.300 --> 00:23:37.850
tooku ga mieru yo PANORAMA mitai sa
Now I can see so far ahead, an unfolding panorama.

00:23:37.850 --> 00:23:43.730
doko kara mite mo heiwa-na Happy Island
Wherever I watch from, I see a peaceful, happy island.

00:23:43.730 --> 00:23:45.270
One more chance

00:23:45.270 --> 00:23:52.910
kimi ni oshietai kimi ni tsutaetai
The thing I want to tell to you, the thing I want to show to you

00:23:52.910 --> 00:23:58.830
yume no GEITO ga me no mae de
The shining gate to our dreams lays open to us...

00:23:58.830 --> 00:24:02.630
ima hiraku yo
right now before our eyes.

00:24:07.140 --> 00:24:12.050
This story is fiction...

00:24:07.140 --> 00:24:12.050
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:15.810 --> 00:24:20.520
Her name is Momoko Sakurayama. She's a
journalist who always pushes the envelope!

00:24:20.520 --> 00:24:23.280
Hey, Noa, she wants
to do a story on you!

00:24:23.280 --> 00:24:30.030
I'm not ready for this!
I don't like this idea! Why choose me?

00:24:30.030 --> 00:24:32.400
Yeah, they should've chosen someone
else. Why don't you just turn it down?

00:24:32.400 --> 00:24:34.910
I'll take the challenge! I'll do it.

00:24:34.910 --> 00:24:39.130
Next episode: The Working Woman.
Target, locked on!

00:24:37.290 --> 00:24:43.080
Next episode

00:24:37.290 --> 00:24:43.080
